<title>SWEDEN: Vattenfall says buys 10.5 percent of NESA.</title>
<headline>Vattenfall says buys 10.5 percent of NESA.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1996-09-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish power generation and distribution group Vattenfall said on Monday it had bought 10.5 percent of the shares in Danish electricity distribution firm NESA A/S.  </p>
<p>The move was a long-term investment which would strengthen Vattenfall's cooperation with the regional power distributor Sjaellandske Kraftwerker, Vattenfall said in a statement.</p>
<p>&quot;NESA is the largest owner of Sjaellandske Kraftwerker and Vattenfall's interest in NESA will deepen this cooperation further,&quot; Vattenfall president Carl-Erik Nyquist said.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom, +46-8-700 1006</p>
